+// The area-light half of GetPhysicalLightAttenuation, for the scene-referred path only
+// (decisions/s8-light-units.md part 2). An area light gets its own inverse square from the LTC
+// form factor - E ~ A*cos*cos/d^2 - so the (r/d)^2 above is a SECOND one, and CE's area lights
+// therefore fall off as d^-4: 1.0 stop under a point light at 2 m, 5.6 stops at 10 m.
+//
+// The radius fadeout is kept, and must be: it is what makes the light reach exactly zero at its
+// clip radius, and without it an area light pops at the tile boundary (research §4 trade-off 3).
+// Squared, exactly as the stock function squares it, so the two agree at the boundary.
+half GetAreaLightFadeout(half fDist, half fInvRadius)
+{
+	const half radius = 1 / fInvRadius;
+	half fadeoutFactor = saturate((radius - fDist) * (fInvRadius / 0.2h));
+	return fadeoutFactor * fadeoutFactor;
+}
